### Test Circle Comment Endpoints
### Replace {{baseUrl}} with your backend URL (e.g., http://localhost:3000)
### Replace {{accessToken}} with a valid JWT access token
### Replace {{circleId}} with "The Void" circle ID from seed script

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@accessToken = YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
@circleId = 6970ba160248543dcec12bb2

### 1. Get Circle Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/circles/{{circleId}}

### 2. List Circle Comments (no auth required)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/circles/{{circleId}}/comments?limit=20

### 3. Create Circle Comment (requires auth)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/circles/{{circleId}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "This is a test comment from the API. The void is listening..."
}

### 4. Create Reply to Comment (requires auth)
### Replace {{commentId}} with an actual comment ID from step 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/comments/{{commentId}}/replies
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "This is a test reply. Echoing into the void..."
}

### 5. List Replies for a Comment
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/comments/{{commentId}}/replies?limit=50

### 6. Delete Comment (requires auth and ownership)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/comments/{{commentId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
